    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-130020",
      "knowledge_point_id": "8505beff-75b8-57bf-9312-e0fcf32f44fd",
      "knowledge_point": "Using Additivity of Double Integrals",
      "problem": "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=12,\\,{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A=-8,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A & =3{∬}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({∬}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(12-8) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
