  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14099948",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-129193",
      "knowledge_point_id": "77be6032-ec22-5561-94c2-be289e343142",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding a Level Surface of a Function Passing Through a Point",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the level surface for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{{z}^{2}}$ that passes through the point $P(1,0,-1).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0,-1) & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{{z}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(1,0,-1)$ is the cone ${z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
        "version": "revealed-ma-answer-v1",
        "feedback_sha256": "e71c68012360db36f98347654257e911d99d2ac0138c6908e42734df16600cf6"
      },
      "difficulty": "moderate",
