  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-40727",
      "knowledge_point_id": "2e891363-fea2-5de4-9bbb-67fddb077200",
      "knowledge_point": "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral When the Limits are Given",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085/assets/0e05b575c22c78000a1ec235bb82cbfad3cd0cdfc6db370f19f094799b305949.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed by the curves $y=2{x}^{2}$ and $y=1+{x}^{2},$ as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type I region. To determine the lower and upper functions, we draw a vertical arrow through the region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14100085/assets/da2895c09bc33f628626257b6d102e74875825df14ba744904e02ffa71552a02.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dy]dx\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{1+{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{2{x}^{2}}f(x,y)\\text{ }dy]dx",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source_answer_policy": {
        "version": "revealed-ma-answer-v1",
        "feedback_sha256": "d5a25b5d7496a4e6b4a19c94b2bb1851baf07b2b5757fe0d407a1633abaa1454"
      },
      "difficulty": "easy",
